WEBVTT

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:55.890
Engine room. Lay smoke screen. Smoke screen, sir.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:00.580
Commander Wisdom.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:02.140
A tanking cruiser, four times.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:08.730
Very good, Bennington.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:10.890
Bearing, sir, 20 degrees.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:12.130
Left half order.

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:13.190
Left half order.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:37.470
- Torpedo control, the fire went on.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:41.510
- Torpedo control?

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:56.030
- Torpedo fired, sir.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.720
- Four torpedoes fired, sir.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:10.250
It hits him.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:11.230
Very good.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.090
Pete will sure put that cruiser out of action.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.560
Aircraft. Fire when ready.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:10.940
All right, sir.

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:11.960
Big time, of course.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:20.550
Waited another second. That bomb would have had us.

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:23.650
Listening force reports submarine, sir, off the starboard bow.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:29.200
Stand by for depth charges.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:30.000
Depth charges.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:30.780
Charge stations.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:42.020
Depth charges, one, two, and three fired, sir.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:45.480
Right, full runner.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:46.400
Right, full runner.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:58.010
Admiral Warburton, you're to be congratulated on the manner in which your fleet has conducted

00:04:58.010 --> 00:04:58.610
these maneuvers.

00:04:58.910 --> 00:04:59.390
Thank you, sir.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:00.000
Commander Warburton.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.420
Winslow is also to be commended.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:02.680
I agree with you, sir.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:05.630
He deserves a lot of credit for the way he's readjusted himself

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:09.260
after being transferred back to his command from naval intelligence.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.520
Order Commander Winslow aboard. I want to talk to him.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:12.220
Aye, aye, sir.

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:14.920
Have that signal sent to Commander Winslow at once.

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:32.100
Penny.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:33.030
Yes, sir.

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:36.210
Take a look at this.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:39.860
Perfect score.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:42.650
Now to knock a couple years off our grades.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:46.040
Won't hurt us, Eddie, especially with the sinkers watching maneuvers.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:50.010
Commander Winslow, Admiral Warburton's compliments, sir.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:51.690
You're to come aboard flagship immediately.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:52.510
Very well.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:55.790
This is red.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:57.260
Cross your fingers.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:58.200
You said it, Don.

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:00.000
And don't forget to present...

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.600
Lieutenant Pennington's compliments to the sinkers.

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:08.970
Commander Winslow reporting, sir.

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:15.680
Commander, I've sent for you to congratulate you on the skillful handling of your ship during the maneuvers.

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:16.560
Thank you, sir.

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:19.490
But the officers and enlisted men deserve most of the credit.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:20.950
I'm glad you realize that.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:25.060
We commanding officers must never forget that it's the spirit of the entire personnel

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:27.580
that makes our Navy the great force that it is.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:30.570
Excuse me, sir.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:42.880
Commander.

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:43.960
Thank you, sir.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:48.010
Supply ship SS Quarter Queen sunk off Tangita Island.

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:50.980
Suspect organized sabotage.

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:55.470
Respectfully request Commander Winslow be transferred back to my division at Pearl Harbor.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.880
Signed, Captain Holding, Naval Intelligence.

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:18.920
Queen is a second supply ship that's been lost attempting to reach Tangier Island.

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:23.560
The first animation that we've had to sabotage is this report from Miss Mercedes Colby.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:24.620
Mercedes Colby?

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:28.160
Yes, she and her friend, Mr. Gay, were the only survivors of the Court of Queen.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:28.900
Do you know them?

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:29.900
Very well.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:30.920
I've worked with them before.

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:33.090
They're both very intelligent girls.

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:34.350
Well, they're more than that.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:35.390
Especially Misty.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:37.500
Well, tell me, Captain.

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:39.580
What were they doing on the Court of Queen?

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:41.580
Well, Miss Gay is secretary to Blake,

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:43.880
the contractor building the naval base at Tangita.

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:47.310
Miss Colby is the head nurse at the new naval dispensary on the island.

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:49.440
What's so important about Tangita?

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:51.540
Well, although it's off the main trade routes,

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:54.580
the trolls based there can protect our shipping lanes.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.570
Then the destruction of these supply ships

00:07:56.570 --> 00:07:58.320
is the work of saboteurs determined

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:00.000
to prevent our building of base on 10 G.

00:08:00.190 --> 00:08:00.750
That's right.

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:05.450
The fact that the quarter queen was torpedoed proves that the saboteurs must have a base

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:07.050
somewhere in the vicinity of Tangita.

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:09.860
That's why I'm sending you there, Winslow, to try and find that out.

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:11.150
We'll do our very best, sir.

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:12.210
I know you'll do that.

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:13.910
Now here's the island layout.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:20.680
Here at the northern tip is a gold mine.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:25.310
The only through road runs south from it, past this native village, to round down a bay

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:26.370
where the base is being built.

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:29.460
You're southbound for Tangita tonight, Commander.

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:29.960
Under.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.300
force draft. Aye, aye, sir.

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:33.070
And good luck. Thank you, sir.

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:49.320
You'll be pulling him around down the bay in less than an hour.

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:52.540
You'll be in command of the ship, Grady, while Lieutenant

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:54.540
Pennington and I are ashore. Aye, aye, sir.

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:57.490
First assignment will be to sail

00:08:57.490 --> 00:08:58.990
directly south 200 miles.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.380
and circle the island, closing in until you return to run down the bay.

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:04.080
Yes, sir.

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:08.190
Tangita looks peaceful enough.

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:08.960
Yeah.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:56.400
U.S. Navy, all right.

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:05.910
And with Winslow on Tangita, we'd better watch our step.

00:10:06.150 --> 00:10:06.850
Know what brought him yet?

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:07.250
Certainly.

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:10.910
To investigate the report that the Court of Queen was torpedoed off this island.

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:16.290
Tracker's carelessness in allowing those two girls to escape when he sank the Court of Queen may disrupt our whole layout here.

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:22.000
I'd hate to be in Tracker's shoes when the Scorpion finds out that Winslow has been sent to Tangita.

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:23.950
Anyway, we have the edge on Winslow.

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:24.930
What's that?

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:27.230
We know something about him and his capabilities.

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:29.410
He doesn't know us or ours.

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:32.460
Someone's leaving the ship.

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:33.340
Who is it?

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:36.750
Looks like Winslow and some of his naval intelligence associates.

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:44.770
Lower the upper periscope.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:12.760
M-22. Get rid of Winslow before you can locate our underwater submarine base.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:14.720
And bring a flock of U.S. destroyers down on us?

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:15.640
No, Pimple.

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:19.280
Scorpion has too big and too costly a layout here to take that chance.

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:20.410
Hey, wait a minute.

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:23.090
Tranker on the Z-37 now.

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:45.150
You'll have to wait until the undersea's oil wells are paired.

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:47.950
That's what keeping Redderton and Miss Z-52 in port.

00:11:48.090 --> 00:11:50.430
As a matter of fact, Franker, you're to keep your sub here in this cave

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:52.890
until you receive further instruction from the Scorpion.

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:54.670
But I don't understand that.

00:11:55.010 --> 00:11:57.590
But it might help your understanding to know that those two girls

00:11:57.590 --> 00:11:59.310
whom you allowed to escape from the court of Queen

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.560
John Winslow and that U.S. destroyer anchored out in the bay.

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:43.810
Stay here, Pindle.

00:12:43.810 --> 00:12:45.330
One of us is enough to greet Winslow.

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:03.890
Look, who's here?

00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:08.400
You'd better stay ashore with us and look out to the radio.

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:09.040
Aye, aye, sir.

00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:09.990
Greg.

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:17.670
Hello, Misty.

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:18.550
It's good to see you.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:19.270
Hi, sailor.

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:20.030
Hi, Misty.

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:21.070
How's the shipwrecked mermaid?

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:22.170
I want to forget about it.

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:22.810
It was pretty horrible.

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:25.080
Here's my boss, Mr. Blake.

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:25.960
I don't think you've met him.

00:13:26.260 --> 00:13:27.440
Welcome to Tangita, Commander.

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:28.410
Thank you, Mr. Blake.

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:30.000
I'm glad to meet you, and I'm glad to be here.

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:31.420
And this is Lieutenant Pennington.

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:32.360
Glad to know you, Lieutenant.

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:35.840
Your job will be a lot easier with Don Winslow and Red Pennington on the island.

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:37.820
To say nothing of the 620 standing by.

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:39.280
I don't doubt it.

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:40.880
We've heard of Winslow even in Tangita.

00:13:41.060 --> 00:13:41.960
Nothing bad, I hope.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:43.560
May I welcome the new arrivals?

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:44.140
Hello, Merlin.

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:47.300
Oh, Commander Winslow, Lieutenant Pennington, this is Mr. Merlin.

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:48.420
Glad to meet you, Mr. Merlin.

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:50.980
Mr. Merlin is the manager of the Tangita gold mine.

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:51.740
Oh, I see.

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:55.540
Commander Winslow is here to investigate the sabatoires that's been holding up my work.

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:57.230
Oh, that's good news.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:14:00.000
Be sure to let me know, Commander, if there's anything I can do to help you.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.180
Thank you, Mr. Merlin. I will.

00:14:01.890 --> 00:14:05.330
Well, Commander, I'd like to show you the officers we've arranged for you in our headquarters.

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:07.190
Oh, I'm sure you'll like them, especially the radio.

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:09.110
Well, sounds very good. Let's look it over.

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:09.850
Okay.

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:29.720
Set. Maybe we can learn Winslow's immediate plans.

00:14:46.220 --> 00:14:48.140
I've been waiting two days for a message from the Baratavia.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:50.360
The Baratavia? Is she headed for Tangina?

00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:52.620
Yes, with equipment, skilled technicians, and their families.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:56.040
My work on the new naval base is practically at a standstill until she arrives.

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:57.700
Well, that looks like our first job, Red,

00:14:57.980 --> 00:14:59.810
is to see that the Baratavia reaches here safely.

00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:01.300
620 will see her through.

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:14.990
Find out the Baritavia's position.

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:16.610
Special code.

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:18.920
Not a good that special code will do with this hookup.

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:20.610
We'll take care of the Baritavia.

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:22.590
You're not risking a submarine to get the Baritavia.

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:24.710
That depends on what Winslow does with the 620.

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:27.550
Spike, you've got an important job for you to do.

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:29.320
Quarry, stick close to that dictaphone.

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:30.000
I want a record.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:31.610
